# ---- Martha's conversation ----
dialogue.harvest_feast_host.off_season.text = The feast's over for this year, and the table's packed away.\nCome back when the fields are in.
dialogue.harvest_feast_host.meet_arrival.text = You walked all that way on an empty stomach, I can tell.\nI'm Martha. When the fields are in I cook for whoever turns up, and the bread comes first. We'll start you on <b>wheat</b>.
dialogue.harvest_feast_host.meet_arrival.opt.hail = Pleased to meet you, Martha.
dialogue.harvest_feast_host.first_words.text = Mind the table, it's longer than it looks.\nEvery year when the fields are in, I set it up here in the <color is="#ffd97a">Forgotten Temple</color> and feed whoever turns up. There's a lot of cooking between now and the feast. You look like you could carry a sack of flour.
dialogue.harvest_feast_host.first_words.opt.hail = Happy to help.
dialogue.harvest_feast_host.board_fresh.text = Board's up. Fields or kitchen, it all needs doing, and it all pays.
dialogue.harvest_feast_host.board_fresh.opt.board = Show me the board.
dialogue.harvest_feast_host.board_fresh.opt.later = Later.
dialogue.harvest_feast_host.board_fresh_friendly.text = Wipe your boots. I saved you a chair.\nThere's an extra job on the board with your name on it.
dialogue.harvest_feast_host.board_fresh_honored.text = Oh good, it's you. Take your pick off the board before the others get to it.
dialogue.harvest_feast_host.board_fresh_revered.text = Sit. Eat something first, you look half starved.\nThe board will keep.
dialogue.harvest_feast_host.menu.text = Mind the pot. What can I do for you?
dialogue.harvest_feast_host.wheat_offer.text = Bread first. It always is.\nThe wild <b>wheat</b> grows thick in the open fields this time of year. Pick me a good armful for the ovens.
dialogue.harvest_feast_host.wheat_offer.opt.accept = I'll bring wheat.
dialogue.harvest_feast_host.wheat_brief.text = <b>Wheat</b> grows wild out in the open fields. Pick it by hand and bring it here.
dialogue.harvest_feast_host.wheat_ready.text = That's a fine armful. The flour will be ground by morning.\nNow, a feast needs a roast. Come back when you're ready to go hunting.
dialogue.harvest_feast_host.wheat_ready.opt.turnin = Here's the wheat.
dialogue.harvest_feast_host.turkeys_offer.text = The <b>Wild Turkeys</b> are out in the woods this month, fat and loud and not as daft as they look.\nBring a few down. The table's no good without a roast.
dialogue.harvest_feast_host.turkeys_offer.opt.accept = I'll go hunting.
dialogue.harvest_feast_host.turkeys_ready.text = You smell like the woods. Good, that means it went well.\nHere's a recipe for the next job. And hold still: if you're going to chase turkeys all week, you might as well look like one.
dialogue.harvest_feast_host.turkeys_ready.opt.turnin = Back from the hunt.
dialogue.harvest_feast_host.pie_offer.text = Your turn at the stove. Learn that recipe, then bake a <b>pumpkin pie</b> at a <b>Chef's Stove</b>.\nDough, a pumpkin, a pinch of spice and a hot oven. Bring it to me.
dialogue.harvest_feast_host.pie_offer.opt.accept = I'll bake you a pie.
dialogue.harvest_feast_host.pie_brief.text = Learn the recipe, then bake a <b>pumpkin pie</b> at a <b>Chef's Stove</b>. You'll want dough, a pumpkin and some spice.
dialogue.harvest_feast_host.pie_ready.text = Smell that. That's a pie somebody cared about.\nYou've done your share and more. Come and sit down; it's time we ate.
dialogue.harvest_feast_host.pie_ready.opt.turnin = Here's the pie.
dialogue.harvest_feast_host.feast_offer.text = Once a year we put it all on the table and eat till nobody can stand.\nBring me a <b>pumpkin pie</b>, some <b>cooked meat</b> and a basket of <b>carrots</b>, and we'll set it out together.
dialogue.harvest_feast_host.feast_offer.opt.accept = Let's set the table.
dialogue.harvest_feast_host.feast_brief.text = A <b>pumpkin pie</b>, <b>cooked meat</b> from the fire and <b>carrots</b> from the fields. Then we eat.
dialogue.harvest_feast_host.feast_ready.text = Pie, roast and carrots. Now that's a feast.\nSit, eat, and take this plate home with you. It's got the year on it, so you'll remember.
dialogue.harvest_feast_host.feast_ready.opt.turnin = Here's everything.
dialogue.harvest_feast_host.feast_done.text = Still full? So am I. The table stays set until the feast is over.\nWhat can I do for you?
dialogue.harvest_feast_host.daily_turkeys_offer.text = Yesterday's roast went down to the last bone. Bring me a few more <b>Wild Turkeys</b> and I'll start another.
dialogue.harvest_feast_host.daily_turkeys_offer.opt.accept = I'll go hunting.
dialogue.harvest_feast_host.daily_wheat_offer.text = Every loaf I baked today is already gone. More <b>wheat</b>, or there's no bread in the morning.
dialogue.harvest_feast_host.daily_wheat_offer.opt.accept = I'll bring wheat.
dialogue.harvest_feast_host.daily_roast_offer.text = Cook some <b>meat</b> over a fire and bring it here. People keep eating it before it gets to the table.
dialogue.harvest_feast_host.daily_roast_offer.opt.accept = I'll bring a roast.
dialogue.harvest_feast_host.active_generic.text = Go on, then. I'll keep a plate warm.
dialogue.harvest_feast_host.ready_generic.text = Let me see what you've brought.
dialogue.harvest_feast_host.ready_generic.opt.turnin = It's done.
dialogue.harvest_feast_host.who_are_you.text = Nobody important. I cook.\nWhen the fields are in, I come here, set out the long table and feed whoever turns up. Some years that's a dozen people. Some years it's everyone for miles.
dialogue.harvest_feast_host.about_feast.text = It's a thank-you, mostly. The fields gave us plenty, and the least we can do is eat it together.\nYou bring something, you take something home. That's all the rules there are.
dialogue.harvest_feast_host.opt.returned = I'm back.
dialogue.harvest_feast_host.opt.quests = What needs doing?
dialogue.harvest_feast_host.opt.board = What's on the board?
dialogue.harvest_feast_host.opt.shop = Let's see your stall.
dialogue.harvest_feast_host.opt.standing = How do we stand?
dialogue.harvest_feast_host.opt.almanac = Show me the Almanac.
dialogue.harvest_feast_host.opt.who = Who are you?
dialogue.harvest_feast_host.opt.feast = What's the feast for?
dialogue.harvest_feast_host.opt.back = Something else.
dialogue.harvest_feast_host.opt.farewell = See you at the table.

# ---- The shared meal and the invitation tour ----
quest.harvest_feast_shared_meal.title = The Shared Table
quest.harvest_feast_shared_meal.flavor = Nobody eats alone at my table. Roast a vegetable over a fire, bring it here, and sit down a while.
quest.harvest_feast_invitations.title = The Guest List
quest.harvest_feast_invitations.flavor = A long table's no good half empty. Go and invite a few people to the feast, then come and tell me who's coming.
objective.harvest_feast.invite = Invite {0} people to the feast
dialogue.harvest_feast_host.meal_offer.text = Nobody eats alone at my table.\nRoast a <b>vegetable</b> over a fire and bring it here, and we'll share it. Come by every day if you like. There's always a chair.
dialogue.harvest_feast_host.meal_offer.opt.accept = I'll bring something.
dialogue.harvest_feast_host.meal_brief.text = Any <b>vegetable</b> will do. Roast it over a fire and bring it to the table.
dialogue.harvest_feast_host.meal_ready.text = Sit, sit. Pass that here and have some of mine.\nThere. Now you've eaten properly today.
dialogue.harvest_feast_host.meal_ready.opt.turnin = Let's share it.
dialogue.harvest_feast_host.invitations_offer.text = A long table's no good half empty.\nGo and tell folk about the feast, anybody who'll stop for a word. <b>Invite a few people</b>, then come back and tell me who's coming.
dialogue.harvest_feast_host.invitations_offer.opt.accept = I'll spread the word.
dialogue.harvest_feast_host.invitations_brief.text = Talk to folk, anybody but me, and <b>invite them to the feast</b>. Start with the ones about the temple; they've worked all week and nobody's asked them yet. Come back once you've asked a few.
dialogue.harvest_feast_host.invitations_ready.text = That many? I'd best bake more bread.\nThank you. A full table's the whole point.
dialogue.harvest_feast_host.invitations_ready.opt.turnin = They're coming.
dialogue.harvest_feast_invitation.opt.invite = Come and eat with us at Martha's table.

# ---- The feast's villagers: Tomas the Miller, Elsie the Weaver and Bram the Shepherd ----
dialogue.harvest_feast_miller.off_season.text = The feast's packed away, and so's the flour.\nI'll be back with more when the fields come in next year.
dialogue.harvest_feast_miller.off_season.opt.farewell = Until next year, then.
dialogue.harvest_feast_miller.greeting.text = Don't stand too close, the flour gets on everything.\nI've hauled sacks up from the mill all week so the ovens never go cold. I could do with a seat at the long table once the feast gets going.
dialogue.harvest_feast_miller.mill.text = Down by the river, same as ever. The wheel turns whether I'm there or not.\nThis time of year every sack it grinds goes to the feast.
dialogue.harvest_feast_miller.opt.mill = Where's your mill?
dialogue.harvest_feast_miller.opt.back = Fair enough.
dialogue.harvest_feast_miller.opt.farewell = I'll let you get back to it.
dialogue.harvest_feast_weaver.off_season.text = The feast is over and the cloths are folded away.\nCome and find me when the fields are in again. I will have new ones by then.
dialogue.harvest_feast_weaver.off_season.opt.farewell = I'll look out for them.
dialogue.harvest_feast_weaver.greeting.text = I have been at my loom since dawn. It is good to stand somewhere else for a change.\nI wove the cloths for the long table. It would be nice to sit down at the feast and eat off one of them for once.
dialogue.harvest_feast_weaver.cloth.text = A runner for the middle of the table, wheat gold with an orange edge.\nSomebody always spills gravy on it, so I weave a new one every year.
dialogue.harvest_feast_weaver.opt.cloth = What are you weaving now?
dialogue.harvest_feast_weaver.opt.back = It's lovely work.
dialogue.harvest_feast_weaver.opt.farewell = I won't keep you.
dialogue.harvest_feast_shepherd.off_season.text = Feast's done. I'm off back up the hill before the sheep wander any further.
dialogue.harvest_feast_shepherd.off_season.opt.farewell = Safe walk home.
dialogue.harvest_feast_shepherd.greeting.text = Came down from the hills with fleece for the weaver. The sheep can look after themselves for a few days.\nThey can't, really. But I wasn't going to miss the feast.
dialogue.harvest_feast_shepherd.sheep.text = My sister. She says she doesn't mind.\nThat means I'm taking her back a whole pie.
dialogue.harvest_feast_shepherd.opt.sheep = Who's watching your sheep?
dialogue.harvest_feast_shepherd.opt.back = She's earned it.
dialogue.harvest_feast_shepherd.opt.farewell = Enjoy the feast.
